WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.750
This is the full tutorial
of how to use Quickler.

2
00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:08.600
I'll go through every button, every setting,
and every combination, explaining as we

3
00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:11.610
go how to use everything on Quickler.

4
00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:16.890
We will start our tour of Quickler
from the Quickler homepage.

5
00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:21.800
Normally we would press sign in, but
today we are signing up as a new user,

6
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:24.070
so we're going to press Try Quickler Free.

7
00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:30.750
This takes us to the sign in page, and
we're going to type in an email here.

8
00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:33.250
You could use your work
email or any other email.

9
00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:36.250
Be sure to tick the box to
confirm you are a person.

10
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:43.060
Once you have done so, you can press send
sign in link, and then you should go to check

11
00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:46.940
your inbox and see the link there.

12
00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:51.750
When you click the sign in link for the
first time, you'll be taken to this page.

13
00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:57.180
First, click on settings. This is where
we'll be able to change whatever the company

14
00:00:57.180 --> 00:01:00.090
name is to something that is correct.

15
00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:05.530
So we'll click on the pencil, and
we'll rename this demo company.

16
00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:12.040
We can also include a logo, so if you want
to go onto your files and include a logo,

17
00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:18.320
you can. That will appear here and also
appear on all of your reports that you send to

18
00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:19.120
people.

19
00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:22.970
Now we're going to use an example logo
to demonstrate what a logo looks like.

20
00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:27.060
You can paste that in or you can upload
and drag and drop in the ordinary way,

21
00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:29.440
and you'll see that appears up there.

22
00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:33.530
Now, while we're on the settings
page, we will edit our contact.

23
00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:38.310
I'm the only contact, but if you
click edit, you can change your name.

24
00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:40.590
Quickler is all about the in-person visit.

25
00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:45.880
You walk around, you send photos and send voice
notes, and Quickler handles the processing

26
00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:47.290
of all the information.

27
00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:50.430
Here is a site safety
inspection on WhatsApp.

28
00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:53.200
We'll say what we're
checking and get talking.

29
00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:59.920
Site safety inspection,
please. I'm at home 6 in

30
00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:00.720
a building.

31
00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:04.820
This brings us to the record. If you
don't say something, we don't make it up.

32
00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:07.410
If you do, we don't lose it.

33
00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:13.260
As soon as you've pressed save, you'll be
able to go onto WhatsApp and you will see that

34
00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:16.220
you have a notification from Quickler.

35
00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:25.030
The number you should expect the
notification from is [inaudible].

36
00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:30.830
It will say something like this. Quickler
account for demo company is ready to start.

37
00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:33.350
Now, reply go to begin.

38
00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:38.080
And so you're welcome to do that, but I think
you might find it more useful if you waited

39
00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:39.070
for a moment.

40
00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:44.220
And what are we waiting for? Well, once
you've added your contact, you'll be able to

41
00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:46.050
press your own logo that you've uploaded,

42
00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:47.830
and that will take you to the home screen.

43
00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:53.410
And you'll see that there are no checks yet,
so what we need to do is press [inaudible].

44
00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:56.500
Now, there's two ways we
can add things to here.

45
00:02:56.500 --> 00:03:00.980
We can copy and paste or just
type the questions we would like.

46
00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:06.570
For example, we could ask for,
what is the oil temperature?

47
00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:10.240
Now, you might have a
long list of questions,

48
00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:15.720
in which case you'd be able to go control
all, control paste, but you can also press

49
00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:19.850
this plus or drag in and drop a PDF,

50
00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:23.770
a Word file or any of these
files. Any file is acceptable.

51
00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:29.140
So I'm going to drag in a demo
form, which I have made as a PDF.

52
00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:32.990
Now you can see that it's attached. I'll delete
this question so as not to confuse things,

53
00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:34.980
and then press this continue arrow.

54
00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:38.740
Now, there will be some processing time, but
once that is complete, you will get taken

55
00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:40.030
to the next page.

56
00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:43.310
Every company does things
a little differently.

57
00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:47.650
With Quickler, you can build your
own check with your own questions,

58
00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:52.230
in your own order. Group them into
sections, choose the type of answer,

59
00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:53.920
and set the usual answers.

60
00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:56.710
Then your team can use it
on WhatsApp immediately.

61
00:03:56.880 --> 00:04:00.380
If it's on another app, you
can export your data from it,

62
00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:03.790
or simply upload a
previously completed record.

63
00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:05.970
Quickler will extract
the questions for you.

64
00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:10.870
And once that processing time is
complete, we'll be greeted with this page,

65
00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:14.070
where we can select a name for our check.

66
00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:19.620
Now, this is the name that it will be called
to yourself, to customers and on WhatsApp

67
00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:20.560
when we get there.

68
00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:23.990
So, we can give it a name that
we will recognise for the future.

69
00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:28.250
Now, you'll see here there is a
feature called the usual answer.

70
00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:33.800
When this is off, the only things that are
put into your final report are things that

71
00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:35.970
you have said as you go round.

72
00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:42.070
With the usual answer on, that means
things that you might say every time.

73
00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:47.900
For example, if you're inspecting a kitchen
and you had to think about fire safety,

74
00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:53.540
you might say that used cooking oil is always
stored securely, whether or not you have

75
00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:55.150
actually looked at the cooking oil.

76
00:04:55.220 --> 00:05:00.420
You'll see here that there is a questions
search bar, so we can search for a particular

77
00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:01.220
question.

78
00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:05.720
For example, if we search for site, we'll see
that the one that says site has been highlighted

79
00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:06.520
for us.

80
00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:09.910
And we can press the
cross to get rid of it.

81
00:05:10.420 --> 00:05:14.760
Now, as we go down the page, we'll see that
there are a few things that flash up between

82
00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:15.560
questions,

83
00:05:15.320 --> 00:05:19.750
where it says add a section here, add
a question here, and the same below.

84
00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:26.000
For example, if I press add a question here,
we can make that question what is the height,

85
00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:27.230
and so on.

86
00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:30.510
We can also delete a
question by double clicking.

87
00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:35.070
If we go to the first question, we
have it classified as an answer.

88
00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:39.720
What is an answer? Well, we can click show
me how, and it's very simply something we

89
00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:41.930
say or type or a photo.

90
00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:44.640
There are other types of questions,
and we'll go through them.

91
00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:49.830
Now, the first is the yes no is a
question which is graded as a yes or a no.

92
00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:52.870
A yes is of course positive,
and a no is of course negative.

93
00:05:53.420 --> 00:05:57.870
Yes and no questions can be good or
bad in the context of the question.

94
00:05:57.980 --> 00:06:01.310
For example, is there a
fire? No, that is good.

95
00:06:01.380 --> 00:06:06.850
Or if you had worded the question as is there
no fires present, then that would be yes,

96
00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:08.510
and that's a good thing there.

97
00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:13.920
As we are on this question, we'll
address the in score, no score button.

98
00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:20.340
This makes the answer of this question count
in the final output as part of the score

99
00:06:20.340 --> 00:06:22.330
that grades the entire report.

100
00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:28.050
Some questions have a list of fixed
answers, like the location or type of work.

101
00:06:28.380 --> 00:06:33.270
Or it could be a fire risk assessment
that might be graded as trivial,

102
00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:34.930
tolerable, and so on.

103
00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:40.780
To do that, we can set the answer type to
graded, then choose the words that people will

104
00:06:40.780 --> 00:06:41.580
use.

105
00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:47.220
You can pick a list that you already use,
if you have one, or press add word and type

106
00:06:47.220 --> 00:06:48.020
your own.

107
00:06:48.320 --> 00:06:51.910
Add the best answer first
and the worst answer last.

108
00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:54.670
Click any word to write what it means.

109
00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:56.850
That sentence then goes to the record.

110
00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:02.350
If you leave a words meaning empty, Quickler
will write one for you shortly after.

111
00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:07.800
The cross beside a word gets rid of it, or
perhaps you'd rather a grade with a number.

112
00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:12.130
Then in that case you can choose
numbers and set the highest number.

113
00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:14.750
On site, nobody will see this list.

114
00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:19.770
They'll just say it in their own words
and Quickler will pick the matching word,

115
00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:21.470
that is the matching grade.

116
00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:27.490
You can open the key at the bottom of the
record to see every word and what it means.

117
00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:32.650
You can change a word sentence here, and
it changes on every record of that check.

118
00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:37.260
The key is printed on your PDF as
well, so readers can see it too.

119
00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:39.790
Or hide it by pressing hide.

120
00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:42.950
You can press it again to show it.

121
00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:45.790
There is also the option of a number.

122
00:07:45.960 --> 00:07:51.570
This allows you to give a figure, such
as 67, and you can even add units.

123
00:07:52.100 --> 00:07:55.170
You'll see here that the usual
answer box is down there as well.

124
00:07:55.500 --> 00:08:00.950
So for example, if this was a question
about what is the weight of the lift,

125
00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:06.040
we could have this question saying
the weight of the lift is 1000kg,

126
00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:09.980
which would mean that the usual
answer would become the answer

127
00:08:09.980 --> 00:08:13.830
unless we state the lift mass
is something other than 1000kg.

128
00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:19.110
Moving down the types of answer, we go
on to date, which is simply the date.

129
00:08:19.780 --> 00:08:24.730
The next thing is a signature, which is a
way of adding an e-signature [inaudible].

130
00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:30.040
The next type of question is location, which
uses your location pin to gather the address.

131
00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:35.120
We also have weather, which uses the location
to get the weather from your local area

132
00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:36.130
instantaneously.

133
00:08:36.880 --> 00:08:42.050
Now you'll also see that we can make
things parents or leave families.

134
00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:47.970
So if I click make parent, you'll see that it
creates the questions below it into a child.

135
00:08:48.260 --> 00:08:54.150
If we want to make this question
not part of the parent above it,

136
00:08:54.180 --> 00:08:57.020
we can press leave
family and it jumps out.

137
00:08:57.020 --> 00:09:02.780
If we scroll down a little, we can have the
question down here join the family above

138
00:09:02.780 --> 00:09:04.190
by clicking join family.

139
00:09:04.340 --> 00:09:09.270
We can also make it a child of the
question above by clicking make child.

140
00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:16.100
If we're not happy with the location
of a question within a question set,

141
00:09:16.100 --> 00:09:19.150
we can use these buttons to change that.

142
00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:25.760
Now you'll see the up and down arrow that
moves the parent up or down relative to others.

143
00:09:25.760 --> 00:09:31.250
So if I press down here, you'll see that we
have moved this question and its children,

144
00:09:31.280 --> 00:09:32.630
which come with it.

145
00:09:32.660 --> 00:09:35.290
If you move a parent, the children
tend to move with parents.

146
00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:39.330
Within families, you can
also move questions around.

147
00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:45.880
For example, this is a child along with
this being a child of the one above.

148
00:09:45.880 --> 00:09:49.270
We can move them up or
we can move them down.

149
00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:54.420
Before we press continue, we will press
these switches, which are not necessary,

150
00:09:54.420 --> 00:09:59.630
but some people like to use them
where you have a particular answer,

151
00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:03.370
which you would like to use when
a particular issue comes up.

152
00:10:03.840 --> 00:10:08.360
This typically makes sense when you're quoting
a regulation or some other kind of guidelines

153
00:10:08.360 --> 00:10:09.790
that you want to cite.

154
00:10:10.520 --> 00:10:14.690
Open any check and press edit and
you land on its overview page.

155
00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:19.400
Duplicate makes a copy you can rename
and change without touching the original.

156
00:10:19.400 --> 00:10:24.890
Edit questions says need setup
until your check has some questions.

157
00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:30.440
Question sources show where your questions
came from, like a PDF or a document that you

158
00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:31.240
uploaded.

159
00:10:31.320 --> 00:10:36.980
The written report turns each record into a
finished document in a PDF or a Word document

160
00:10:36.980 --> 00:10:39.990
laid out in sections like any report.

161
00:10:40.480 --> 00:10:44.540
Edit where answers go shows where
each answer lands in that layout.

162
00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:50.390
Under who and when, phone access sets
the times this check can be done.

163
00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:53.470
Contacts sets who this check is for.

164
00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:59.750
If you choose nobody, then anyone with a
phone number on your account can do it.

165
00:11:00.180 --> 00:11:05.580
If you choose people with a phone number, only
those people you select can do it on WhatsApp

166
00:11:05.580 --> 00:11:06.380
or Telegram.

167
00:11:06.840 --> 00:11:09.500
If you choose people who
have emails on the account,

168
00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:16.410
they will get sent an email with the
record when tell managers is turned on.

169
00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:19.890
Several people can do the
same check at the same time.

170
00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:23.030
Send now sends the check to
one person straight away.

171
00:11:23.580 --> 00:11:27.790
Something urgent, like a safety fault,
is sent to managers straight away.

172
00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:31.410
To tidy up your checks on the
homepage, you can use a folder.

173
00:11:31.780 --> 00:11:35.680
If you press new folder, you'll be
able to give it a name and save it.

174
00:11:35.680 --> 00:11:40.810
You can drag a check into a folder
and back out if you don't need to.

175
00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:43.430
You can rename a folder or delete it.

176
00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:46.310
The checks and records
inside are never deleted.

177
00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:50.170
Some answers are worked out for
you, like a total or a date.

178
00:11:50.620 --> 00:11:56.930
On a number question, you can press add
sum and say in words what needs adding.

179
00:11:57.280 --> 00:12:00.340
You can then press enter and
Quickler turns it into a sum.

180
00:12:00.340 --> 00:12:06.300
On the record, the answer is worked out and
you can still edit it, should you need to

181
00:12:06.300 --> 00:12:07.100
do so.

182
00:12:07.360 --> 00:12:11.290
Many reports have standard paragraphs
which you write again and again.

183
00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:16.430
By sending them to Quickler once, they'll appear
in the record automatically when appropriate.

184
00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:20.470
So your standard wording is always
there, but never where it doesn't belong.

185
00:12:21.220 --> 00:12:25.340
You've probably already spent years
getting your report to look just right.

186
00:12:25.340 --> 00:12:27.540
With Quickler, you don't
have to change them.

187
00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:32.290
Send us a finished report as a
Word document, PDF or even a photo,

188
00:12:32.320 --> 00:12:36.670
and every new record comes back in
that layout with your headings, tables,

189
00:12:36.820 --> 00:12:37.730
logos and footers.

190
00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:41.590
You can even use a different logo
on a single check if you need to.

191
00:12:42.060 --> 00:12:44.250
Adding someone to Quickler takes seconds.

192
00:12:44.560 --> 00:12:46.650
All you need is their name
and their phone number.

193
00:12:46.860 --> 00:12:49.830
There's no app for them to download
and no password to remember.

194
00:12:50.040 --> 00:12:53.910
When the time comes to do a check,
they need only ask Quickler for it.

195
00:12:54.420 --> 00:12:56.510
Many checks happen on a routine.

196
00:12:56.840 --> 00:13:01.160
Tell Quickler which days and times you need
it and it will send the check to your team

197
00:13:01.160 --> 00:13:02.290
whenever you choose.

198
00:13:02.560 --> 00:13:07.010
If someone hasn't done it, they'll get
a reminder and their manager is told.

199
00:13:07.140 --> 00:13:09.970
If you need something done
today, just send it now.

200
00:13:10.820 --> 00:13:12.970
Nobody loves another app on their phone.

201
00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:19.800
Therefore Quickler works on WhatsApp, the
same app that 90% of people in the UK already

202
00:13:19.800 --> 00:13:20.600
have.

203
00:13:20.220 --> 00:13:24.230
There is nothing to download
and no login for your team.

204
00:13:24.900 --> 00:13:28.830
If they know how to send a message,
they know how to use Quickler.

205
00:13:29.180 --> 00:13:32.810
There are few things more annoying
than typing during a visit.

206
00:13:32.960 --> 00:13:36.870
With Quickler, you can send a voice
note just like you would to a friend.

207
00:13:37.100 --> 00:13:42.060
Quickler can transcribe any accent and puts
each thing you said on the right question

208
00:13:42.060 --> 00:13:43.110
in your report.

209
00:13:43.880 --> 00:13:46.630
Often when you're visiting somewhere,
you'll need to take photos.

210
00:13:46.660 --> 00:13:49.260
You can send them straight
to Quickler on WhatsApp.

211
00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:51.910
There's no need to say
what the photos are for.

212
00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:55.050
Quickler works it out and puts
each photo where it belongs.

213
00:13:55.180 --> 00:13:58.950
If one does land in the wrong place,
just drag it to the right one.

214
00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:03.390
That change is logged and used to
improve Quickler for you next time.

215
00:14:04.100 --> 00:14:07.230
On a visit, things rarely
happen in the order of a form.

216
00:14:07.340 --> 00:14:10.830
With Quickler, you can answer in
the order that suits you best.

217
00:14:10.920 --> 00:14:15.830
Whether that's a text message, a voice note,
a photo, a document or even your location.

218
00:14:16.040 --> 00:14:18.840
Quickler will put each one
of these in the right place.

219
00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:25.360
For sharing your location on an Android
device on WhatsApp, the steps are pretty

220
00:14:25.360 --> 00:14:26.160
simple.

221
00:14:26.520 --> 00:14:31.030
First, you must press the paper clip
down at the bottom of your screen.

222
00:14:31.160 --> 00:14:35.770
We'll then open a menu like
this, where we select location.

223
00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:39.970
This will then open the
map as you see before you.

224
00:14:40.200 --> 00:14:44.560
If you're on a site right now,
press send your current location.

225
00:14:44.560 --> 00:14:51.700
If you are not at the site, but
you'd like to select that site

226
00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:52.500
address,

227
00:14:52.960 --> 00:14:58.370
you can press the button in the top left
that expands the map to full screen.

228
00:14:58.820 --> 00:15:01.280
From there, you'll see a red
pin in the centre of your screen

229
00:15:01.280 --> 00:15:04.750
and you can choose to move
that wherever you need.

230
00:15:05.180 --> 00:15:09.210
You can even put it down on a
specific bus stop should you need to.

231
00:15:09.580 --> 00:15:11.840
Once you have selected
where your pin would be,

232
00:15:11.840 --> 00:15:15.010
you can press on the pin and
press send this location.

233
00:15:15.620 --> 00:15:19.940
Quickler will use that pin you have sent to
get the weather and your address from that

234
00:15:19.940 --> 00:15:20.740
location.

235
00:15:21.080 --> 00:15:25.030
This is how to send your
location to Quickler on Telegram.

236
00:15:25.560 --> 00:15:28.530
It's very similar to WhatsApp where
you first press the paper clip.

237
00:15:29.000 --> 00:15:33.490
From there, you'll see in the
bottom bar the location option.

238
00:15:33.680 --> 00:15:34.570
Select that.

239
00:15:35.120 --> 00:15:37.160
From there, you can select
your current location

240
00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:42.170
and you can also choose other
locations should you need to.

241
00:15:42.780 --> 00:15:48.750
On Telegram, there's the extra
benefit which is like iOS on WhatsApp.

242
00:15:49.420 --> 00:15:50.350
You can do this as well.

243
00:15:50.580 --> 00:15:57.360
You can change the base map to satellite
which allows you to choose very specific

244
00:15:57.360 --> 00:15:58.160
items.

245
00:15:58.240 --> 00:16:00.730
For example, this allotment in Dundee.

246
00:16:01.180 --> 00:16:04.960
You can then send that selected
location and the process is done.

247
00:16:04.960 --> 00:16:10.240
On an iPhone using WhatsApp, tap
the plus, then select location

248
00:16:10.240 --> 00:16:13.130
and finally select your current location.

249
00:16:13.360 --> 00:16:17.810
Sometimes you may need to send a
signature as part of your report.

250
00:16:18.520 --> 00:16:22.570
With Quickler, you can do that through
Telegram or WhatsApp by using a photo.

251
00:16:22.900 --> 00:16:24.030
I'll show you how.

252
00:16:24.300 --> 00:16:29.700
First, press the camera button on the chat
and then take a photo of something plain.

253
00:16:29.700 --> 00:16:35.190
This could be your hand or a piece of
clothing or the ground or something like that.

254
00:16:35.340 --> 00:16:37.850
I'm taking a photo of the
desk in this situation.

255
00:16:38.640 --> 00:16:40.330
Then press the photo button.

256
00:16:40.660 --> 00:16:42.640
Once you've done that, select the pen.

257
00:16:42.640 --> 00:16:45.330
You'll see on WhatsApp the
pen is in the top right.

258
00:16:45.780 --> 00:16:47.730
You can choose any colour you want.

259
00:16:48.080 --> 00:16:49.230
I'm going to go for bright green.

260
00:16:49.800 --> 00:16:52.270
And then write your signature.

261
00:16:52.820 --> 00:16:54.550
Once you've done that, press done.

262
00:16:54.600 --> 00:16:57.800
I should say the rotation that you
send your signature in doesn't matter

263
00:16:57.800 --> 00:17:00.410
because Quickler will
correct that for you.

264
00:17:00.700 --> 00:17:01.670
You don't have to say anything.

265
00:17:01.940 --> 00:17:03.770
It will be recognised as a signature.

266
00:17:04.120 --> 00:17:06.180
And you can go on with
your check as normal

267
00:17:06.180 --> 00:17:10.170
or if you're just coming to the
end, you can say done as usual.

268
00:17:10.940 --> 00:17:15.350
As you go round a site, it's easy to lose
track of what you have and haven't said.

269
00:17:15.540 --> 00:17:18.750
After every message, Quickler
replies with what's still to cover.

270
00:17:18.800 --> 00:17:20.810
That way you always know what's left.

271
00:17:21.540 --> 00:17:24.200
On a visit, you usually
only mention what's wrong.

272
00:17:24.200 --> 00:17:28.830
So Quickler automatically assumes
anything you don't mention is OK.

273
00:17:29.140 --> 00:17:34.110
Quickler reads each question to work out
whether a place might simply not have it.

274
00:17:34.200 --> 00:17:39.070
For example, if your report asks about solar
panels, most buildings don't have them.

275
00:17:39.100 --> 00:17:42.710
So if they're not mentioned, Quickler
marks them as not applicable.

276
00:17:42.900 --> 00:17:46.970
And of course, you can always change
any answer in the record afterwards.

277
00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:51.300
It's very likely you'll visit somewhere
with no internet connection at some point.

278
00:17:51.300 --> 00:17:55.510
Whether that's a multi-storey car
park, a tunnel or a remote project,

279
00:17:55.560 --> 00:17:58.990
you can just carry on sending your
messages and photos as normal.

280
00:17:59.240 --> 00:18:02.530
WhatsApp will then send them
as soon as you're back online,

281
00:18:02.660 --> 00:18:05.870
just like your messages come through
when you turn off flight mode.

282
00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:11.050
After 15 minutes, if you forget to say
done, Quickler will remind you to do so.

283
00:18:11.120 --> 00:18:14.830
And if you still forget, the
record will file after 12 hours.

284
00:18:15.340 --> 00:18:17.250
When you are finished, just say done.

285
00:18:17.420 --> 00:18:19.700
That's how Quickler knows
your inspection is over.

286
00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:22.510
Nothing gets filed until you say it.

287
00:18:22.900 --> 00:18:27.540
Then Quickler sorts all your photos and
all the words into the right places,

288
00:18:27.540 --> 00:18:29.270
ready for you to improve.

289
00:18:29.780 --> 00:18:33.990
Imagine you've just said done to
Quickler and your record is filing.

290
00:18:34.300 --> 00:18:38.570
You're back at the car and you notice a
fault as you leave that you didn't mention.

291
00:18:38.900 --> 00:18:42.030
Just tell Quickler straight
away and the record is amended.

292
00:18:42.160 --> 00:18:44.370
That way, nothing gets left out.

293
00:18:45.180 --> 00:18:48.160
Every fault you mention goes
straight into the to-do list.

294
00:18:48.160 --> 00:18:52.250
It sits at the top of the record,
so nobody has to hunt for it.

295
00:18:52.340 --> 00:18:55.910
You can reword a line, hide
one, or change the order.

296
00:18:56.100 --> 00:19:01.160
And when the person receiving the report gets
it, they can copy and paste wherever it's

297
00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:01.960
needed.

298
00:19:02.360 --> 00:19:04.650
With Quickler, you are always in control.

299
00:19:04.840 --> 00:19:08.930
Once we've written the report, you
can click any answer to edit it.

300
00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:13.460
All edits save as you go, whether you've
changed a word, a sentence, or a paragraph.

301
00:19:13.460 --> 00:19:18.640
Quickler also learns your habits and the
changes you make to make things easier in the

302
00:19:18.640 --> 00:19:19.440
future.

303
00:19:19.880 --> 00:19:24.670
Every word on a record can be
changed before it goes out and after.

304
00:19:24.900 --> 00:19:26.970
But nothing is changed without trace.

305
00:19:27.300 --> 00:19:31.590
Every edit is kept in the record's
history with who made it and when.

306
00:19:31.800 --> 00:19:35.390
That way, you can always see
exactly what was changed.

307
00:19:35.840 --> 00:19:39.560
Every record keeps the whole chat it came
from attached at the bottom of the record.

308
00:19:39.560 --> 00:19:44.050
That is every message, photo, voice note, and
any documents with the time they were sent.

309
00:19:44.240 --> 00:19:47.990
So if anyone ever asks where the
data came from, you can show them.

310
00:19:48.700 --> 00:19:50.870
Every report has its own shareable link.

311
00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:54.960
It can be copied and sent to anyone,
whether that's a client, your boss,

312
00:19:54.960 --> 00:19:56.190
or a site manager.

313
00:19:56.380 --> 00:20:00.150
They can open it on any device,
without needing a login or an app.

314
00:20:00.360 --> 00:20:02.930
It's view-only, so they
can't change anything.

315
00:20:02.980 --> 00:20:05.920
And the link always shows
the record as it is now.

316
00:20:05.920 --> 00:20:10.290
So if you need to change something,
their copy will be updated straight away.

317
00:20:11.080 --> 00:20:15.500
Many people receiving the report will still
want to download and keep the files for their

318
00:20:15.500 --> 00:20:16.300
own records.

319
00:20:16.480 --> 00:20:21.910
That's why Quickler lets them download
a PDF, a Word document, Excel, a CSV,

320
00:20:22.000 --> 00:20:23.270
or even a web version.

321
00:20:23.520 --> 00:20:28.080
Imagine you have a week's worth of inspections,
or one big site that took several days

322
00:20:28.080 --> 00:20:28.990
to get round.

323
00:20:29.100 --> 00:20:32.480
Either way, you'll want one record
that brings them all together.

324
00:20:32.480 --> 00:20:35.750
On the checks record page, press combine.

325
00:20:36.160 --> 00:20:39.670
Then click the records you
want, by subject or by person.

326
00:20:39.800 --> 00:20:42.610
Take a group, and everything
in it comes as well.

327
00:20:42.820 --> 00:20:47.600
Quickler then makes them into one combined
record, kept under combined records on that

328
00:20:47.600 --> 00:20:48.400
page.

329
00:20:48.360 --> 00:20:52.170
If the records are all from the same
place, like a daily check of one building,

330
00:20:52.280 --> 00:20:53.670
the latest answer counts.

331
00:20:53.960 --> 00:20:57.740
If they're from different places,
like separate buildings on a big site,

332
00:20:57.740 --> 00:21:02.220
the worst answer is the one that's flagged,
and the fault always says which place it

333
00:21:02.220 --> 00:21:03.020
came from.

334
00:21:03.160 --> 00:21:06.750
Any photo that turns up more
than once appears only once,

335
00:21:06.760 --> 00:21:11.760
and the combined record lists exactly what
it was made from, so you can always find the

336
00:21:11.760 --> 00:21:12.560
originals.

337
00:21:12.620 --> 00:21:16.670
So whether you need one report for a
large site, or one for the whole week,

338
00:21:16.740 --> 00:21:18.090
it only takes a few clicks.

339
00:21:18.360 --> 00:21:19.530
Quickler has you covered.

340
00:21:19.980 --> 00:21:24.040
Every check has a records page, with
everything it has ever collected.

341
00:21:24.040 --> 00:21:30.590
Once you have enough records, filters
appear, today, 7 days, 30 days and so on.

342
00:21:31.020 --> 00:21:36.770
You can switch between by subject and by
person to see the same records another way.

343
00:21:37.140 --> 00:21:42.030
You can click a title, and you see its
whole history, one record after another.

344
00:21:42.780 --> 00:21:47.610
You can press download all, and choose
a file type for every record at once.

345
00:21:48.240 --> 00:21:51.760
Quickler packs them into a zip
with each record in its own folder.

346
00:21:51.760 --> 00:21:58.000
You can also open any record, and add more
photos, or drag them to where they belong,

347
00:21:58.000 --> 00:21:58.800
like this.

348
00:21:59.240 --> 00:22:02.870
When you click on a photo,
you can turn it, like this.

349
00:22:03.400 --> 00:22:07.610
You can change its caption here,
and type what you like, like this.

350
00:22:08.020 --> 00:22:11.430
Or you can copy it by
clicking here, like this.

351
00:22:11.660 --> 00:22:14.730
Or you can archive it, if you
don't want it on the record.

352
00:22:15.160 --> 00:22:19.360
An archived photo waits all the
way down here, at the bottom.

353
00:22:19.360 --> 00:22:22.270
You can bring it back by clicking here.

354
00:22:22.560 --> 00:22:27.750
A document sent during the walk, much
like a PDF, is kept with the record too,

355
00:22:28.100 --> 00:22:28.930
down here.

356
00:22:29.220 --> 00:22:33.490
Press edits and time to see how
long the walk and edits took.

357
00:22:33.920 --> 00:22:39.090
To delete a record, press delete,
then confirm in the box that it opens.

358
00:22:39.700 --> 00:22:43.850
You get about 10 seconds to press undo,
and the record comes straight back.

359
00:22:44.200 --> 00:22:48.700
Even after that, a record is kept
for 30 days after being deleted,

360
00:22:48.700 --> 00:22:50.850
so if you need it, just ask us.

361
00:22:51.180 --> 00:22:53.490
Every product on site
needs a COSHH assessment,

362
00:22:54.180 --> 00:22:57.810
and that usually means an evening at
the desk with a safety data sheet.

363
00:22:58.760 --> 00:23:01.010
Here I did three in under three minutes.

364
00:23:01.540 --> 00:23:06.830
As you can see, I said new COSHH,
sent the safety data sheet,

365
00:23:07.440 --> 00:23:12.490
sent a short voice note saying how
it's used, and then I said done.

366
00:23:13.160 --> 00:23:16.260
Then I moved straight on to the
next one, and did the same again.

367
00:23:16.260 --> 00:23:21.370
New COSHH, new SDS, a new
voice note and said done.

368
00:23:21.940 --> 00:23:24.630
And then I did the exact
same thing a third time.

369
00:23:25.080 --> 00:23:28.380
While I was doing this, all
three were being written up,

370
00:23:28.380 --> 00:23:31.080
a few minutes later they
all appeared together

371
00:23:31.080 --> 00:23:34.750
with all the ingredients, hazard
controls and safety gear filled in.

372
00:23:35.180 --> 00:23:37.970
From here I can then download
them in different formats,

373
00:23:38.360 --> 00:23:42.900
including a Word document in
the client's own report layout.

374
00:23:42.900 --> 00:23:45.950
If you have to do a
site safety inspection,

375
00:23:46.200 --> 00:23:50.600
with Quickler you can walk the site and send
photos and voice notes on WhatsApp as you

376
00:23:50.600 --> 00:23:51.400
